{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And Abraham bowed before the people of the land.</b> He bowed to give them thanks, acknowledging that for their honor Ephron agreed to grant his request — as they said, of blessed memory (Kiddushin 31a): one who hears his father being honored by others does not say 'they hurried for my own sake' but 'they hurried for my father's sake; they exempted me for my father's sake.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:13.349721658Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}